From dbbc128e2dd96a01f0e9cbcbf85e63d7b4b2183e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calogero Mandracchia <calogero@efebia.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:38:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] rmcp-client: hand subscribed custom server notifications
 to their subscriber

The client handler ignores custom notifications. A caller can now subscribe
to one method before initialize and receive its notifications in a bounded
queue, in the order the server sent them: they are taken from the transport,
before the SDK dispatches each notification in a task of its own. A full
queue drops new ones.
